WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.525
Each of these dangers
has a guard in the code.

2
00:00:02.525 --> 00:00:07.262
The biggest is treating the matrix's
proposal as the owner's decision, so they

3
00:00:07.262 --> 00:00:12.075
live in separate files, and the check
flags every account until its owner signs.

4
00:00:12.075 --> 00:00:15.500
A guess about where a workload
runs gets no proposal at all.

5
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.525
Learn's limits on delegated accounts
are enforced, not just noted.

6
00:00:19.525 --> 00:00:23.863
Kerberos accounts can't be kept
forever, high-risk accounts can't wait,

7
00:00:23.863 --> 00:00:26.375
and no wave goes ahead without a way back.

8
00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:30.094
And this code never deletes
anything: retirement still goes

9
00:00:30.094 --> 00:00:34.100
through Chapter 2's rule and the
reviewed decommission process.
